<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says holds release of imported rice.</title>
<headline>Manila says holds release of imported rice.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Bureau of Customs held the release of some 3,000 bags of &quot;illegally imported&quot; rice at the Manila port, state-owned National Food Authority (NFA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The NFA said the imported glutinous rice in bags of 50 kg each, imported from Thailand and Malaysia, arrived in Manila via Zamboanga, Cotabato and Cagayan de Oro in southern Philippines.</p>
<p>The government regulates the importation of rice to protect local farmers.</p>
<p>NFA said it imported a total of 500 tonnes of glutinous rice, which is used in the preparation of various Filipino rice cakes, last year.</p>
<p>&quot;The confiscated rice remains in custody of the  Bureau of Customs but the NFA proposes for the sale through the agency's accredited retailers,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
